data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For each example, $\\ell = \\log(1 + e^{z}) - yz$. Split $\\log(1 + e^{z})$ as $\\max(z, 0) + \\log(1 + e^{-|z|})$, so\nthat every exponential has a non-positive exponent. The mean over examples is the answer. Targets $y$ may be\nany value in $[0, 1]$, because the formula is linear in $y$."},"hints_note":null}

